The deployable/SHIPPED divergence was surfaced by an architecture-review
subagent (finding B4) and confirmed here by set-diffing the two lists, which
now comes out empty both ways.

Not fixed here, from the same review and worth issues of their own:
- The loopback rule in docs/boundaries.org has no enforcing check. Changing
  INADDR_LOOPBACK to INADDR_ANY in all three proxy copies passes all ten local
  gates while publishing an unauthenticated REPL on every interface.
- gmake lint still treats a missing guild as a pass (Makefile:77-82), inside
  checks.
- Makefile:105,109,128 guard with '|| { echo skipping; exit 0; }' on their own
  recipe line; make runs each line in a fresh shell, so exit 0 skips nothing
  and the recipe dies Error 127. Right outcome, wrong reason, lying message.
- docs/surfaces.org contradicts its own table: agents/ and hooks/ are marked
  present in the rows and NOT BUILT in the mermaid 40 lines later.

Version choice: patch rather than minor. No shipped surface gains or loses a
capability; gmake icons is a developer target, and assets/probe-converters.scm
ships only because assets/ is in SHIPPED.
